From dbf85a047705e90ae38a27415fee209bbbea362a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanjay Singh <sanjay@namsconsulting.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 19:05:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tier-1 currency layer, live results, and the last of the
 unverifiable claims
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three things, none of which change any calculation.

1. Claims. The AdSense pass missed a few because they were worded differently
   from the ones I searched for: "SEBI & RBI compliant formulas" (reversed),
   "10,000+ business owners", "25,000+ contractors", "Why Millions Choose
   Numrexo", "trusted by professionals globally", and "all free, all accurate"
   on all 13 category hubs. A four-month-old domain cannot support any of them
   and a reviewer checks exactly this. Compliance claims are replaced with what
   is actually true: the formulas are standard and published, and each page
   shows the one it used.

2. Currency. Every money calculator printed a hard-coded rupee sign while the
   copy around it was written for a US reader — the tipping guide quoted
   rupees next to advice about US cities. lib/currency.ts plus a switcher lets
   the reader choose, defaults to USD, and keeps INR in the list. Nothing is
   converted between currencies; only the label and the digit grouping change.
   Applied to tip, discount, markup and student loan.

3. Results now update as you type on those four pages, instead of sitting
   behind a Calculate button, and each opens on a worked example. The alert()
   popups are gone. Realistic starting values, US figures in the prose.

